{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Natural World"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Fight for the Cause"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No. <br> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really. <br>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I went on an arctic cruise, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would be able to experience nature at its finest.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">an arctic fox appeared,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would be very excited.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I were you,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would save a little money each month towards a cruise.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. You don't need a comma if the condition comes after the result in the sentence. <br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> I'd go on an arctic cruise if I won the lottery tomorrow.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd)."}, {"type": "example", "content": " If nobody cared about narwhals or any other animal in the world, there wouldn't be any animals left to care about!"}, {"type": "example", "content": " If I wanted to do that, I would buy a lottery ticket."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you really wanted to go, you could save enough in a few months. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use modals to give advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most common modals for giving advice are: <span class=\"italic\"> should</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> had better.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. In this case, these modals add the meaning of advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should</span> is the most common modal used to give advice.<br/><span class=\"italic\"> Ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> had better</span> are used for giving strong advice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Modal</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Main Verb</span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">should</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">more about wildlife preservation.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">ought to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">be</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">more careful about disposing of our garbage.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">had better not</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">do</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">more to protect the whales.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li>In conversation, it is common to use contractions with had better.</li> "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "disconnected "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "removed from an issue; out of touch "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I feel so disconnected from the natural world."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about nature."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "documentary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "documentary"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I ought to watch mo